        "reason": "valid",
        "payload": "tree c058eb48150362e0672dbe424de08ebd9fed4723\nparent a527a0077a0fcae913188410214efe98021c0cca\nauthor John Lawniczak <lawniczak.john@gmail.com> 1794585917 -0500\ncommitter John Lawniczak <lawniczak.john@gmail.com> 1794589951 -0500\n\ntest: Cover 64-bit flatfile position boundaries\n\nCheck FlatFilePos serialization against independently encoded 64-bit\npositions at the signed and unsigned 32-bit boundaries and UINT64_MAX.\n\nExercise FlatFileSeq::Open and AutoFile positioning around 2 GiB and\n4 GiB, including position preservation across size(). Keep the file at\none byte by never writing past EOF.\n\nSkip large seeks on non-Windows builds with 32-bit long, where the\ncurrent FileSeek64 wrapper still uses fseek. Serialization coverage\nremains enabled.\n\nFollow-up coverage for bitcoin/bitcoin#36669.\n",
